          "text": "Dear Patient,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with typical absence seizures, with onset at age 13 years. Seizures currently occur approximately twice per month. The epilepsy is categorized as genetic, with a causative **PCDH19** variant, **c.918G>A**. The epilepsy is drug responsive. MRI demonstrates nonspecific white matter changes.\n\n**Current Medications:**  \n- Lamotrigine — current  \n- Lacosamide — current  \n\n**Seizure Burden Summary:**  \nTypical absence seizures, approximately 2 per month.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nGeneralized epilepsy with typical absence seizures, onset at age 13 years, genetic etiology associated with **PCDH19 c.918G>A**, currently drug responsive. MRI shows nonspecific white matter changes.\n\n**Plan:**  \nContinue documentation of seizure frequency and ongoing management with the current antiseizure medications: lamotrigine and lacosamide. Continue epilepsy clinic follow-up.",
